From 0bf401d1a634314b629d592dd8098a850a738358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:19:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aros: preserve the main process directory before starting GUI
 workers

Problem: ABIv11 crt.library stores chdir's original lock in the shared CRT
base, but restores it on the main process at shutdown. If the GUI worker
calls chdir first (including through realpath), CRT saves the worker's lock
and later unlocks the main process's Workbench startup lock. fromwb then
unlocks that freed lock again. RAM filesystem lock sharing can hide this.
Scope: PdfCraft's AROS GUI entry point, before any application workers.
Use the public chdir API; do not modify the SDK or private CRT fields.
Failure to preserve the directory stops startup before workers are created.
Mainline: fromwb still retains and unlocks its original lock. Mainline's
pthread/CRT thread hooks differ; this is an ABIv11 application adaptation,
not a replacement for those hooks or a general thread-safe chdir fix.
Verification: tests/workbench-cwd compares the saved CRT lock against the
main process's original lock, with and without the initialization.
Upstream-status: local; candidate for the AROS frontend.
---
 apps/pdfcraft-aros/src/main.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apps/pdfcraft-aros/src/main.rs b/apps/pdfcraft-aros/src/main.rs
index bc1472b..08e0993 100644
--- a/apps/pdfcraft-aros/src/main.rs
+++ b/apps/pdfcraft-aros/src/main.rs
@@ -176,6 +176,15 @@ fn save_prefs(app: &PdfCraftApp) {
     }
 }
 fn main() {
+    // ABIv11 CRT shares chdir's saved directory across pthreads, but restores it
+    // on the main process at exit. Save this process's original lock before a
+    // worker's realpath/chdir can save its own. Otherwise CRT frees the lock
+    // that Workbench startup will later UnLock again. chdir(".") preserves the
+    // directory while giving CRT a replacement lock it owns.
+    if let Err(error) = std::env::set_current_dir(".") {
+        eprintln!("pdfcraft: cannot preserve startup directory: {error}");
+        std::process::exit(1);
+    }
     let requesters = pdfcraft_aros_runtime::suppress_requesters();
     install_logger();
     #[cfg(all(target_os = "aros", feature = "diag-alloc"))]
